# DESTINATION: the www-data crontab
#   sudo crontab -u www-data -e          # paste the ONE uncommented line below
#   sudo crontab -u www-data -l          # verify it is installed
#
# Run it as www-data — the same user as PHP-FPM and the Horizon unit — so that every log and
# cache file the scheduled commands touch keeps one owner. A scheduler running as root or as
# your SSH user will create root-owned files in storage/logs and the web worker then cannot
# write to them.
#
# ONE cron line drives ALL NINE scheduled commands. Laravel's scheduler is a single dispatcher:
# cron wakes `schedule:run` every minute and it decides what is due.

* * * * * cd /var/www/careos && php artisan schedule:run >> /dev/null 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PATH WARNING. Three documents (DEPLOY-RUNBOOK.md:363, DEPLOY-CHECKLIST.md:229,
# DEPLOY-READINESS-CHECK.md:156) say /var/www/careos. The code comment at routes/console.php:23
# says `cd /srv/careos` and is the outlier. Copying that one produces a cron line that cd's
# into a directory which does not exist, so the whole line is a silent no-op — cron reports
# nothing and every scheduled command below simply never runs. Use the path where you actually
# installed the app, and verify with the "DID IT FIRE" check at the bottom.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# THE NINE SCHEDULED COMMANDS — read off routes/console.php at 73d8ed9.
# Every one is ->withoutOverlapping() and ->onOneServer(). None uses ->runInBackground(), so
# they execute sequentially inside the schedule:run process.
#
#  cadence        command                             what it does / WHAT STOPS WITHOUT THE CRON
#  -------------- ----------------------------------- --------------------------------------------
#  daily 01:30    audit:verify-chains                 Walks each ACTIVE tenant's append-only audit
#                 (routes/console.php:107-110)        hash chain and prints `CHAIN:OK <slug> (<n>
#                                                     events)` per tenant. WITHOUT IT: tampering or
#                                                     corruption of the PHI audit ledger is never
#                                                     detected. This is the compliance backstop.
#
#  daily 02:10    credentials:refresh-status          Recomputes staff credential/licence status
#                 (routes/console.php:44-47)          (valid / expiring / expired). WITHOUT IT:
#                                                     expired clinical licences keep reading as
#                                                     valid and nobody is warned.
#
#  daily 02:20    nursing:materialize-visits          Materialises Spitex/home-care visits from
#                 (routes/console.php:51-54)          recurring plans over a rolling 8-week horizon.
#                                                     WITHOUT IT: the dispatcher board empties out
#                                                     as the existing horizon is consumed — planned
#                                                     visits simply stop appearing.
#
#  daily 02:30    clinical:evaluate-recalls           Evaluates recall due dates. WITHOUT IT: no
#                 (routes/console.php:57-60)          patient recall ever becomes due, so recall
#                                                     letters and lists stay empty.
#
#  daily 05:30    hospital:accrue-bed-days            Captures each active inpatient stay's per-diem
#                 (routes/console.php:65-68)          bed-day charge through the billing engine
#                                                     (idempotent). Deliberately BEFORE the billing
#                                                     sweeps so the day's bed-days are in first.
#                                                     WITHOUT IT: inpatient billing silently
#                                                     UNDER-CHARGES, every day, with no error.
#
#  daily 06:00    billing:dunning-run                 Generates dunning letters. WITHOUT IT: overdue
#                 (routes/console.php:72-75)          invoices are never chased.
#
#  daily 06:30    billing:reconcile                   Reconciliation sweep; raises and clears the
#                 (routes/console.php:81-84)          reconcile alarm. WITHOUT IT: a billing
#                                                     discrepancy never raises its alarm, so the
#                                                     figures drift unnoticed.
#
#  every 15 min   appointments:dispatch-reminders     ENQUEUES due appointment reminders. It does
#                 (routes/console.php:89-92)          not send them — it dispatches
#                                                     SendAppointmentReminderJob onto redis
#                                                     (Modules/Scheduling/src/Services/
#                                                     ReminderDispatcher.php:93-94). The actual send
#                                                     happens in the queued job, so REMINDERS NEED
#                                                     BOTH THIS CRON AND A RUNNING HORIZON.
#                                                     WITHOUT IT: no patient is ever reminded.
#
#  every 5 min    scheduling:expire-waitlist-offers   Expires stale waitlist offers. WITHOUT IT:
#                 (routes/console.php:97-100)         offers never time out, so slots stay held by
#                                                     patients who never responded.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWO THINGS THAT ARE **NOT** SCHEDULED — operator decisions, not oversights to fix blindly
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 1. audit:ensure-partitions is NOT registered anywhere. DEFERRED.md:156-157 records it as the
#    one scheduler item never wired. The two deploy docs disagree about how much that matters:
#    DEPLOY-CHECKLIST.md:234-235 calls it a go-live gate ("add the line before go-live") while
#    DEPLOY-READINESS-CHECK.md:334 marks it "*(Optional, S1)*". Neither supplies a cron line.
#    It DEGRADES rather than fails — a p_max catch-all partition absorbs rows past the last
#    defined partition — so nothing breaks; the audit table just stops being neatly partitioned.
#    If you want it, add a SECOND crontab line (monthly, well clear of the 01:30 chain check):
#
#      17 3 1 * * cd /var/www/careos && php artisan audit:ensure-partitions >> /dev/null 2>&1
#
# 2. horizon:snapshot is NOT registered either, although config/horizon.php:148-158 configures
#    metrics retention that assumes it ("trim_snapshots"). Consequence: the Horizon dashboard's
#    Metrics tab never populates. Nothing else is affected. To enable it:
#
#      */5 * * * * cd /var/www/careos && php artisan horizon:snapshot >> /dev/null 2>&1
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DID IT FIRE? — a missing or wrong cron line is SILENT. Nothing errors; things just never
# happen. There is no live heartbeat, so check it deliberately after install:
#
#   php artisan schedule:list      # shows all nine with their next due time
#   sudo crontab -u www-data -l    # the line is actually installed
#
# Then wait five minutes and confirm a side effect — the every-5-minute waitlist sweep is the
# fastest signal. Do NOT rely on storage/logs alone: the schedule line discards all output.
